       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose is above the maximum for metformin.\n\n- **Ordered:** 1700 mg three times daily, which is 5,100 mg/day.\n- **Labeled maximum:** 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin. Extended-release is typically capped at 2,000\u20132,550 mg/day. The usual maximum single dose is 850\u20131,000 mg.\n- **Risk:** The ordered amount is about twice the maximum daily dose. That raises the risk of GI toxicity and lactic acidosis, even with normal renal function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day)\n- 1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals (2,000 mg/day)\n- 1,700 mg PO total per day, for example 850 mg twice daily\n\nIf you do want 1,700 mg three times daily, tell me and include a short note on the clinical rationale. I'll enter it with that note. Otherwise, tell me which dose to enter."
      }
